==============================================================================
[3] what this does to the wind
==============================================================================
    Section 2 needs an uncertainty on the shape relation. This measures only
    one part of it -- the ambiguity in reading L/B off a perimeter at all --
    and that alone is already:
      U = 1.5 m/s (elasticity 0.843) -> sigma(U) >=   7.9 %
      U = 2.0 m/s (elasticity 1.159) -> sigma(U) >=   5.8 %
      U = 2.5 m/s (elasticity 1.468) -> sigma(U) >=   4.6 %
      U = 3.0 m/s (elasticity 1.769) -> sigma(U) >=   3.8 %
      U = 3.5 m/s (elasticity 2.062) -> sigma(U) >=   3.2 %

    and the fuel-to-fuel variation in the relation itself, the suppression
    that shaped these perimeters, and the mapping error in them are all on top.

